5. **Minor, new. TIGHTEN:** “The Second Circuit counts Executive Branch practice over thirty years and across five administrations, and it says the Justice Department understood the detention statute the same way when it issued that rule.” The top and figure have established the practice; the institutional history slows the rehearing passage.

6. **Minor, new. CUT:** “A motion to extend the time to respond was granted in Lopez-Campos, and Buenrostro-Mendez was rescheduled.” Those docket mechanics change none of the unresolved questions the preceding sentences answer.

