The highest remaining reader question is **whether Barbosa da Cunha is still on bond now**. The [appeals opinion](/Volumes/4/GitHub/the-catch-site-wt-detention/data/sources/immigration-detention/ca2-cunha-opinion-2026-04-28.txt) says an immigration judge “released him on bond.” No checked later record establishes his current custody status. This bears on answer **2**; the page reports the release but does not state current status as unknown. It displaces no numbered edit, and I would not add a custody claim without a record.

There is no other record-backed answer hole requiring added copy. In particular, the page states that the detention count is unknown and distinguishes it from the Fourth Circuit’s count of cases.

